  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING OF COMMUNITY OF PRACTICE MEMBER ORGANISATIONS TOWARD ENDING GBV IN COMMUNITIES &#x2013; (END-GBV)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of this project is to eliminate all forms of gender-based violence against girls and women in Sierra Leone. The project has 3 objectives: (1) enhance the institutional capacity of the Community of Practice (COP) and member organisations to effectively address Gender-Based Violence (GBV) in the Western Area, Bo, Bombali, Falaba and Karene districts; (2) Community structures served by the COP demonstrate increased knowledge of GBV laws and issues facing them; (3) Community structures served by the COP member organisations demonstrate increased capacity and actions to combat GBV and promote community awareness and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
